        "question_text": "<p>For the reaction $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$, what is the effect of increasing the pressure on the equilibrium position?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>According to Le Chatelier's Principle, increasing the pressure shifts the equilibrium to the side with fewer moles of gas to reduce the pressure. Here, the left side has 4 moles of gas ($1 N_2 + 3 H_2$), and the right side has 2 moles ($2 NH_3$). Thus, the equilibrium shifts to the right.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
